I did a bit more digging and maybe a better solution would be to add the following comment that disables typescript errors for the next line

{noformat}// Temporary fix for strictNullChecks. Please remove this comment block and fix the typescript error
// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/ban-ts-comment
// @ts-ignore: strictNullChecks error <error message>{noformat}

Example:


{noformat}        // Temporary fix for strictNullChecks. Please remove this comment block and fix the typescript error
        // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/ban-ts-comment
        // @ts-ignore: strictNullChecks error TS2531: Object is possibly 'null'.
        if (providerPrice < this.usageConditions.min_provider_price) {
            return this.inactivateCampaign();
        }{noformat}

The plan is:
1. Enable strict null checks
2. Compile the code and get a list of errors
3. Add comment before each line to ignore the typescript errors

This would allow us to enable {{strictNullChecks}}for the entire microservice and slowly fix the existing code base. The only drawback is that {{//@ts-ignore}}ignores _all_ ts errors.



