[~accountid:5eb93ce06c84140b9eaa367f] - apologies for the delay in coming back to you with regard to the T&Cs. Do you have any specific questions regarding the T&Cs?

From my side, they are broadly fine and a few things to note:

* 4.6 - lost, stolen or duplicated cards and compromised PINs - must be notified asap - otherwise we will be liable to pay for any transactions made in these circumstances and our account will continue to be topped up automatically, so this is risky; 
* 5.1(d) - the list price for fuel products and any charges can be changed unilaterally by HTC and will take effect midnight following the day they were announced; 
* 5.3(e) - any dispute in relation to an invoice has to be raised within 28 days of the date of the invoice, which is pretty reasonable but still FYI especially in relation to the first point raised; 
* 6.4(e) by accepting their terms we are deeming to obtain the consent of each cardholder to the processing of their personal data pursuant to the Agreement - I would suggest that each cardholder will be sent a copy of the T&C’s so they are also aware of this and other terms; 
* 7.1 either party can terminate the agreement on 4 weeks' notice in writing - just FYI; 
* 10.2 - HTC can unilaterally vary the terms which they will post on the online portal - so please monitor it for updates from time to time because the use of a card after any such updates made - will be deemed to be acceptance of modified T&Cs - (not sure this would be compliant with EU consumer protection regulations but nonetheless please monitor this and raise anything you are not sure about). 

