Hey!

Do I understand the following key points correctly?

→ The agreement is made voluntarily, between the employer (Bolt UK) and the employee;

→ The deductions and payments are made by the employer;

→ The payments are made Scottish Widows via AON, who is administering the pension scheme;

→ The agreement can be concluded once a year, during set time-frame and can be terminated before the next accounting period by giving a prior written notice at least 30 days before. After terminating the agreement, no re-enrollment is possible before the start of next accounting period;

→ The payments are made from the employee’s payroll;

→ The payments can be set up as instructed by the employee - from overtime payments, night time fee,  bonuses.

→ Payments can be made either in full or as a percentage;

→ This will affect the gross salary;

→ This will be regarded as change to the existing employment agreement;



# Are we calling this an agreement or opt-in form? 
# Do we have any pre-defined sets of sacrifice that could be listed on template? Or is this made in accordance with the will and wishes of the employee?
# Is the employer making any (matching) contributions?
# Will this affect current pension payments of the employee? Or is this in addition to the existing contributions? 
# Can adjustment be made during the ongoing accounting period? (including/excluding sacrifices)
# Do we have any regulations/guidelines/policies adopted that should be referenced?

Hello,

See my answers in red below:

→ The agreement is made voluntarily, between the employer (Bolt UK) and the employee; {color:#ff5630}*YES*{color}

→ The deductions and payments are made by the employer; {color:#ff5630}*YES*{color}

→ The payments are made to Scottish Widows via AON, who is administering the pension scheme; {color:#ff5630}*YES*{color}

→ The agreement can be concluded once a year, during set time-frame and can be terminated before the next {color:#ff5630}*payroll* {color}period by giving a prior written notice at least 30 days before. After terminating the agreement, no re-enrollment is possible before the {color:#ff5630}*next opt in period organised by Bolt UK once per calendar year; (we will decide the window, but will be 2 weeks in November each year)*{color}

→ The payments are made from the employee’s payroll; {color:#ff5630}*YES*{color}

→ The payments can be set up as instructed by the employee - from overtime payments, night time fee, bonuses.{color:#ff5630}*YES*{color}

→ Payments can be made either in full or as a percentage; {color:#ff5630}*YES*{color}

→ This will affect the gross salary; {color:#ff5630}*No, as overtime payments, night time fees, bonuses are all additional sums to the existing gross salary. When such sums are not awarded by the company, gross salary would not be affected*{color}

→ This will be regarded as change to the existing employment agreement; {color:#ff5630}*No - since bonuses, night time fees or overtime payments are not part of the employment contract but rather discretionary fees awarded by the company (both by the contract templates we have in place in UK as well as UK employment law)*{color}



# Are we calling this an agreement or opt-in form? {color:#ff5630}*I would say it’s an agreement because the opt in form is provided by AON to be completed by employee in order to finalise details once agreement is made*{color}
# Do we have any pre-defined sets of sacrifice that could be listed on template? Or is this made in accordance with the will and wishes of the employee? We suggest offering 3 options, and the employee chooses which one to take: {color:#ff5630}*just to keep the admin minimal I would propose 3 options only, from which employee can choose -*{color} {color:#ff5630}*full amount, 50% or 25%* {color}
# Is the employer making any (matching) contributions? {color:#ff5630}*NO*{color}
# Will this affect current pension payments of the employee? Or is this in addition to the existing contributions? {color:#ff5630}*It’s in addition*{color}
# Can adjustment be made during the ongoing accounting period? (including/excluding sacrifices) {color:#ff5630}*NO, only once a year when we open up the opt in window in November*{color}
# Do we have any regulations/guidelines/policies adopted that should be referenced? {color:#ff5630}*NO, it’s a purely discretionary and voluntary agreement which can be made if both employer and employee agree with the terms, to allow us to administer payroll accordingly for the employee in question*{color}

Hope this helps, let me know if you need further details

